desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Flutterwave Public Key"
	title_zh: "检测到Flutterwave Public Key",
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-secrets-flutterwave-public-key"
	risk: "hardcoded-credentials"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `flutterwave-public-key` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/secrets/gitleaks/flutterwave-public-key.yaml).
Original message: A gitleaks flutterwave-public-key was detected which attempts to identify hard-coded credentials. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module).

CWE: CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials
References:
- https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Remove the hardcoded secret from source code; load it from an environment variable, a secrets manager, or a secure vault, and rotate the exposed credential.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-secrets-flutterwave-public-key
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/(?:FLWPUBK_TEST-(?i:[a-h0-9]{32}-X))|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-secrets\-flutterwave\-public\-key/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Flutterwave Public Key",
	title_zh: "检测到Flutterwave Public Key",
	message: "Flutterwave Public Key",
}
